{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795808599,"nonce":"kX0074NPnfIlgWl3TGjbzU6lzEE=","title":"Dispatch at a bare tag name records it as a branch and passes a branch allowed_refs glob","message":"A manual or API dispatch with a bare ref name (no refs/ prefix) recorded refs/heads/\u003cname\u003e whatever the forge resolved the name to (canonicalize_ref in crates/scarab-server/src/lib.rs), and the fork check (dispatch_is_fork_code) accepted a tag of that name as the repository's own code. A writer could create tag release/evil on their own commit and dispatch ref release/evil: the Run recorded refs/heads/release/evil and passed an Environment's allowed_refs for refs/heads/release/* (and the OIDC subject named that branch). A tag named like an existing branch could likewise be recorded as that branch. HEAD was recorded as refs/heads/HEAD. Reported by the red team on main (0.8.3).","files":null}]}